{
  "$comment": [
    "Measured times of the Go suite under -race (task #174): what scripts/test-shards.mjs rebalance cuts the test units of",
    "scripts/test-shards.json from, and what `estimate` (and web/tests/deploy/testShards.test.ts) holds every -race shard",
    "to RACE_BUDGET_MIN with. Written by `node scripts/test-shards.mjs times --from <logs> --write`; source says from which runs.",
    "files: per cut package, per test file, [seconds its measured tests took, how many were measured] - each test the median",
    "of the runs it ran in. A test file or test added since counts at its package's mean per test.",
    "packages: every other package, its seconds as `go test` printed them (0: no test files).",
    "model: how those seconds become a job's minutes on that runner - setup_min (checkout, toolchain, the -race build:",
    "1.1-2.4 measured, the cut shards' job minus their tests) and package_parallel (go test -p runs packages side by side:",
    "the package shards' summed package seconds over their job minus setup, 3.2-3.6 measured; the lower one is kept).",
    "Re-measure when a release run's -race shard is far from its estimate: docs/CONTRIBUTING.md, Testing -> Shards."
  ],
  "source": "GitHub Actions ubuntu-latest (4 vCPU): the -race jobs of ci.yml's full runs 37624094959 (v0.53.0), 37702037032, 37795793601 (v0.54.0), 37811308088 and 37952392755 (v0.55.0), 2026-10-07 to 2026-10-09, median per test and per package",
  "model": {
    "setup_min": 2,
    "package_parallel": 3.2
  },
